{"title":"Karamata's Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Karamata's Inequality</b> states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77973d910799f2f3cf44b644b4a3238c180f9850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Majorization\" title=\"Majorization\">majorizes</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc3d022be42b3678206917304b0113651bc5c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_function\" title=\"Convex function\">convex function</a>, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a4a83faeec64d121a46b01a9d9e59fa1e01f1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(a_i)\\geq \\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(b_i)\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Karamata%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will first use an important fact:\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is convex over the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704edbf993afa55dff225e32ff390ffb2edab494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall a\\leq x_1\\leq x_2 \\leq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e895f92ad1224fe06f6d193b985c09ffff33b530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma(x, y):=\\frac{f(y)-f(x)}{y-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"181\" height=\"44\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fb097eb847baaa36e58fa67f18426b4d5aa3a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma(x_1, x)\\leq \\Gamma (x_2, x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This is proven by taking casework on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b94c71548f6aea7b231ffd9d612dea7d31b812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq x_1,x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64fcddbd81c14ec6a2659e381b15e19c5702206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba7af700eda7a71cfae06a5a6f2af0cc3e85608.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Gamma(x_1, x)=\\frac{f(x_1)-f(x)}{x_1-x}\\leq \\frac{f(x_2)-f(x)}{x_2-x}=\\Gamma(x_2, x)\\]\" width=\"403\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>A similar argument shows for other values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Now, define a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4a41fcf633cc45fc4b425e36bc9dd9658122df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_i=\\Gamma(a_i, b_i)\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Define the sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63ab8ca2a0e6dabd47a146d887b1aa1edb27cd16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_i=\\sum_{j=1}^{i}a_j, A_0=0\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"52\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f7ff1d2561a1aeb9c1e6a0e4a4cc2da1bab71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> similarly.\n</p><p>Then, assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e85465a9379a0b11dac1233721104b36bd67ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i\\geq a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" /> and similarily with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" />'s, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8af771b01d386b289b90f6ae677d0fafbf010e2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_i\\geq c_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />. Now, we know:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e64c9146d7841436de40d5d5e72757978fdafe3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(a_i) - \\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(b_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(a_i)-f(b_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_i(a_i-b_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_i(A_i-A_{i-1}-B_i+B_{i+1})\\]\" width=\"650\" height=\"47\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba4bc41c9d0d35b27b8ce9431c6c5d39c3f9cf1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_i(A_i-A_{i-1}-B_i+B_{i+1})=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}c_i(A_i-B_i) - \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}c_{i+1}(A_i-B_i)=\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}c_i(A_i-B_i) - \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}c_{i+1}(A_i-B_i)\\]\" width=\"753\" height=\"50\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f7bb1eec5a949d486b9af2e333b6b195dbaa1b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}c_i(A_i-B_i) - \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}c_{i+1}(A_i-B_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(c_i-c_{i+1})(A_i-B_i)\\geq 0\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f3a0bda5405595d581b32b1825d4126963bd36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(a_i) \\geq \\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(b_i)\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we have proven Karamata's Theorem.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Karamata%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Karamata%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 139/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 312/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4924/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.697      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.697      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7267:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018063945 and revision id 217532. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}